 "structural_change": "CODEX HWIN structural SRAM redesign: 16 independent event payload SRAMs (63b due+pos+user) with independent attribute SRAMs; gap and retire timestamp in SRAM. 64x16 true1R1W macros banked84total, registered write ports and previous-write forwarding. Due precomputed at record, final comparator registered due==tm+1. Binary shadow address pointers drive only bank read pins. Kept reset-distinct identity copies <=16entries, per-event reset regions. Remaining parallel identities1457b; fd752bits are fired-state vectors. No extra output edge or change to D>=nw+2. Inactive events enabled only by offset bootword; parameter-free die master16rows. Outline pin/halo constrained475.2x432, macros on43.2grid with10.8halo. Regions successor: same-edge reset-distinct per-event time/wrap/config/address state, per24 RX identity pin copies, registered per12-bit one-hot output selects and endpoint-local collision reductions. All latency edges preserved; strict fanout and actual sizing remain measured gate checks. Central-band geometry successor:8columns x11rows, centralrow skipped for full-width y248.4..291.6 register band. Clock and reset on W beside band; no RTL/reset/data-edge changes. Production parent-fit and measured wire/clock/timing remain owed. HEAD_STAGE=1 captures each fresh head payload unconditionally beside its existing registered winner; output edge and minimum D unchanged. Prune standard rows to the full-width declared band before tapcell. GPL-only row envelope restores full paid physical core and all 84 fixed macro placements before downstream stages. COMPACT_PTR1 uses two reset-distinct same-edge binary pointer copies for two decoder halves. CHECK_STAGE1 evaluates exact next configuration state into local validation flags, preserving first-start fault edge. Default CHECK_STAGE0 remains the direct reference; low/high invalidD fixtures and47slot wrap compare all outputs/faults every cycle.",
 "pin_regs": {
  "enable": false,
  "reason": "Source-registered: f_ks / f_mc / f_mw / mu_rt land in pin flops (ks_q / mc_q / mw_q / rt_q), mu_c / mu_rc / t_wf leave flops (c_q / rc_q / t_wf)."
 },
